              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em Exact couples
            are a way to encode data that makes a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence"} spectral sequence
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fibers"} homotopy fibers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Postnikov+tower"} Postnikov tower
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+tower"} Adams tower
            (see also at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+spectral+sequence"} Adams spectral sequence
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#exact_couples Exact couples
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Given an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+couple"} exact couple
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is a cyclic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence"} long exact sequence
              of three
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              among two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi k
                    %mi E
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi j
                    %mi D
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi φ
                    %mi D
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi k
                    %mi E
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi j
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots \stackrel{k}{\longrightarrow} E \overset{j}{\to} D \overset{\varphi}{\longrightarrow} D \overset{k}{\to} E \overset{j}{\longrightarrow} \cdots
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p This being cyclic, it is usually depicted as a triangle
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi φ
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi j
                            %mo ↖
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi k
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    D &amp;&amp; \stackrel{\varphi}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; D
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{j}}\nwarrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{k}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    E
                    }
          %p
            The archetypical example from which this and the following definition draw their meaning is example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExactCoupleOfATower"}
            below.
          %h3#SpectralSequencesFromExactCouples Spectral sequences from exact couples
          #CohomologySpectralSequence.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em
                cohomology
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence"} spectral sequence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mi r
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{E_r^{p,q}, d_r\}
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a sequence
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msubsup
                          %mi E
                          %mi r
                          %mrow
                            %mo •
                            %mo ,
                            %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{E_r^{\bullet,\bullet}\}
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi r
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℤ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in \mathbb{Z}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi r
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \geq 2
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bigraded+object"} bigraded
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
              %li
                %p
                  a sequence of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentials"} differentials
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi r
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msubsup
                          %mi E
                          %mi r
                          %mrow
                            %mo •
                            %mo ,
                            %mo •
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msubsup
                          %mi E
                          %mi r
                          %mrow
                            %mo •
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                            %mi r
                            %mo ,
                            %mo •
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mi r
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{d_r \colon E_r^{\bullet,\bullet} \longrightarrow E_r^{\bullet+r, \bullet-r+1}\}
            %p such that
            %ul
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi H
                        %mrow
                          %mi r
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mo •
                          %mo ,
                          %mo •
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_{r+1}^{\bullet,\bullet}
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+cohomology"} cochain cohomology
                of
                = succeed ":," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi r
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_r
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi E
                          %mrow
                            %mi r
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                          %mrow
                            %mo •
                            %mo ,
                            %mo •
                        %mo =
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi E
                          %mi r
                          %mrow
                            %mo •
                            %mo ,
                            %mo •
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi r
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_{r+1}^{\bullet, \bullet} = H(E_r^{\bullet,\bullet},d_r)
            %p
              Given a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              = succeed "_" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+abelian+group"} graded abelian group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\bullet
              equipped with a decreasing
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtration"} filtration
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ⊃
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mi s
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo ⊃
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C^\bullet \supset \cdots \supset F^s C^\bullet \supset F^{s+1} C^\bullet \supset \cdots \supset 0
            %p such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo ∪
                      %mi s
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mi s
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi and
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi s
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mi s
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C^\bullet = \underset{s}{\cup} F^s C^\bullet \;\;\;\; and \;\;\;\; 0 = \underset{s}{\cap} F^s C^\bullet
            %p
              then the spectral sequence is said to
              %em converge
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo •
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\bullet
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo ,
                        %mo •
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E_2^{\bullet,\bullet} \Rightarrow C^\bullet
            %p if
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  in each bidegree
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi s
                        %mo ,
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s,t)
                  the sequence
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msubsup
                          %mi E
                          %mi r
                          %mrow
                            %mi s
                            %mo ,
                            %mi t
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mi r
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{E_r^{s,t}\}_r
                  eventually becomes constant on a group
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi E
                          %mn ∞
                          %mrow
                            %mi s
                            %mo ,
                            %mi t
                        %mo ≔
                        %msubsup
                          %mi E
                          %mrow
                            %mo ≫
                            %mn 1
                          %mrow
                            %mi s
                            %mo ,
                            %mi t
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty^{s,t} \coloneqq E_{\gg 1}^{s,t}
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi E
                          %mn ∞
                          %mrow
                            %mo •
                            %mo ,
                            %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty^{\bullet,\bullet}
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+graded"} associated graded
                  of the filtered
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\bullet
                  in that
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi E
                          %mn ∞
                          %mrow
                            %mi s
                            %mo ,
                            %mi t
                        %mo ≃
                        %msup
                          %mi F
                          %mi s
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %mi s
                            %mo +
                            %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %msup
                          %mi F
                          %mrow
                            %mi s
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %mi s
                            %mo +
                            %mi t
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty^{s,t} \simeq F^s C^{s+t} / F^{s+1}C^{s+t}
                  \.
            %p
              The converging spectral sequence is called
              %em multiplicative
              if
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msubsup
                          %mi E
                          %mn 2
                          %mrow
                            %mo •
                            %mo ,
                            %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{E_2^{\bullet,\bullet}\}
                  is equipped with the structure of a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bigraded+object"} bigraded object
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} algebra
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi F
                          %mo •
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^\bullet C^\bullet
                  is equipped with the structure of a filtered
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+algebra"} graded algebra
                  (
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi F
                          %mi p
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi k
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msup
                          %mi F
                          %mi q
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi l
                        %mo ⊂
                        %msup
                          %mi F
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo +
                            %mi q
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %mi k
                            %mo +
                            %mi l
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^p C^k \cdot F^q C^l \subset F^{p+q} C^{k+l}
                  );
            %p such that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  each
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi r
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_{r}
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
                  with respect to the (induced) algebra structure on
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %msubsup
                              %mi E
                              %mi r
                              %mrow
                                %mo •
                                %mo ,
                                %mo •
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {E_r^{\bullet,\bullet}}
              %li
                %p
                  the multiplication on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi E
                          %mn ∞
                          %mrow
                            %mo •
                            %mo ,
                            %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty^{\bullet,\bullet}
                  is compatible with that on
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mo •
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\bullet
          #ExactCoupleAndDerivedExactCouple.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              %strong (derived exact couples)
            %p
              An
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+couple"} exact couple
              is three
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi g
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                            %mo ↖
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi h
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    D &amp;&amp; \stackrel{g}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; D
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{f}}\nwarrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{h}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; E
                    }
            %p
              such that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
              of one is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              of the next.
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi im
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi im
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi im
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    im(h) = ker(f)\,,\;\;\; im(f) = ker(g)\,, \;\;\; im(g) = ker(h)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Given an exact couple, then its
              %em derived exact couple
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi im
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi g
