                    E_\infty^{p,n-p} \simeq F^p G^n / F^{p+1} G^n
                    \\,.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#ExactCoupleOfATowerOfFibrations Exact couple of a tower of (co)-fibrations
          %p
            …
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence+of+a+tower+of+fibrations"}> spectral sequence of a tower of fibrations
            …
          #FilteredSpectrum.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+spectrum"} filtered spectrum
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              equipped with a sequence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo ,
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Spectra
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet \colon (\mathbb{N}, \gt) \longrightarrow Spectra
              of spectra of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 3
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots
                    \\longrightarrow
                    X_3
                    \\stackrel{f_2}{\longrightarrow}
                    X_2
                    \\stackrel{f_1}{\longrightarrow}
                    X_1 \stackrel{f_0}{\longrightarrow} X_0 = X
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              More generally a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} filtering
              on an object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              in (stable or not)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
              is a
              = succeed "-graded" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimit"} homotopy colimit
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ≃
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo ⟶
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mo •
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\simeq \underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim} X_\bullet
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FilteredSpectrum"}
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              There is
              %em no
              condition on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              in def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FilteredSpectrum"}
              %em not
              required to be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-monomorphisms"} n-monomorphisms
              or
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-epimorphisms"} n-epimorphisms
              for any
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %p
              On the other hand, while they are also not explicitly required to have a presentation by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
              or
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structures+for+spectra"} model structures for spectra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
              or by
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
            %p
              This means that we may think of a filtration on a spectrum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              in the sense of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FilteredSpectrum"}
              as equivalently being a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tower+of+fibrations"} tower of fibrations
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            The following remark
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UnrolledExactCoupleOfAFiltrationOnASpectrum"}
            unravels the structure encoded in a filtration on a spectrum, and motivates the concepts of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+couples"} exact couples
            and their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequences"} spectral sequences
            from these.
          #UnrolledExactCoupleOfAFiltrationOnASpectrum.num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+spectrum"} filtered spectrum
              as in def.
              = succeed "," do
